as  also overlooking second avenue and we  were all  very concerned about all this and so and  then my  85 year old sister was staying in  another apartment  that was on the other side of the  building on the back side overlooking  the river  and so we all went down got in the car  and left and we went across the bridge  over to lp field um and  our nissan stadium i keep calling it lp  field it's nissan stadium  and we went over there and sat there for  about 20 minutes  and you could still see your apartment  from where you were at  we could see the back of it yes we  couldn't see the second avenue side we  could see first avenue which those  streets were in parallel to one another  so  um so then we went back  i said well you know clearly this is  nothing's going to happen so  a drove back came back down 2nd avenue  headed north on 2nd avenue and got to  broadway  which is our main thoroughfare through  our entertainment district in nashville  where all the honky tonks are  and um and i was sitting there because  the police did have 2nd avenue blocked  off and i and was trying to decide am i  going to go park car  go back you know and um and and it  exploded and the fireball from that  thing  rose up past the top of the att property  that was sitting there  and and you know i've seen all these  other pictures since  and it completely blew out the entire  front  of the three to four buildings that are  just north of  ours blew out all of our windows blew  out windows  on the back side of the building the  riverside of the building  blew all of those windows out and also  blew windows out  on third avenue which was a block over  so  the windows the windows in your building  were blown out so  what would have happened if you'd have  stayed i would have been killed  i would have been killed i would have  been at the very least  severely injured but because i was  sitting right there i mean we were  we raised the window so we could really  clearly hear  what the rv was saying and to make sure  it was coming from the rv  and it was indeed coming from the rv and  um  and i don't know if you've what pictures  you've seen there was a white car  that was parked a couple of spaces  behind  that rv which was of course destroyed  in the explosion but there was nothing  left of that rv  it it went i mean it completely exploded  i mean i'm sure they'll find  remnants of it but yeah and so the other  thing  you you say was it was outside the att  building i mean  is there anything in that in that area  that could have been a target  i don't i don't know i know that there  are some communications equipment  that there is communications equipment  for that att  has in that building but i don't know  how because they actually moved their  headquarters to what we call the batman  building  in 1996 i think but they still  retain that building over there and i  know that they do have some equipment in  it  it doesn't have any windows they don't  have many people who work over there  you know it's a it's a fairly desolate  uh building  in terms of pedestrian activity and  and all of this and like i said no  windows and  that van that's not van the rv  the was was parked right  there in front of that building and this  rv was an  older model but it was in pristine  condition i mean in terms of looking at  it it was  white white and not any dirt on it  didn't have any markings on it that i  could see when i looked at it  but you know i also i didn't take a  photograph  and why i didn't take a photograph of it  i don't know  because it was just sitting in the  street it's just it's just just a car  you want to know it was going to  go up in flames how long did it take how  long did it take for police to arrive  uh well the police got there fairly  quickly after we  after the 9-1-1 call you know they got  there  they got there pretty quickly they sent  they sent uh  two cars down there i mean you know  it's gunshots and then they got out and  heard that thing  and when that thing started going off  you know we didn't go down we weren't  trying to but because what if there'd  been a gunman on the street  you know so so because that could have  been very  what the scenario was that that was the  one that made the most sense to us  we didn't want to draw attention to our  building up there  you know because i didn't want to get  shot  well we're very glad you're safe and and  thank you so much for talking to us  here at ddw thank you thank you so much  thank you for checking on us okay bye  that's uh betsy  williams and nashville resident  you
 

